  "line_550_warning_analysis": "CodexR3HTTPStreamingTests.swift:550 emits a Swift compiler warning because startLoading() binds `let client = self.client` in the outer DispatchWorkItem and implicitly captures `client` strongly in that finite setup closure while capturing `[weak self, weak client]` in the nested repeating timer closure. Runtime ownership is sound (outer setup work item runs once and exits; repeating timer holds `client` weakly), and capturing `[weak self, weak client = client]` or `[self, client]` in the outer closure eliminates the warning cleanly."
